    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "a066cd6cb907c1947fb018fd23c2e735c41a8d43cc704f98c2bd05a674188956",
      "text": "After breakfast, you’ll set out on a full-day trip to the Pacific coast. The excursion lasts about **8–9 hours**.\n\nThe drive passes olive groves, orchards and vineyards in the Curacaví and Casablanca valleys. The coast is about **120 km** away.\n\nYou’ll spend the first part of the day in Valparaíso. The city is built on 42 hills, with buildings spread across different levels. Its historic quarter is a UNESCO World Heritage Site. Old funiculars, stairways and footpaths connect the city’s different levels.\n\nYou’ll see Plaza Sotomayor and the naval headquarters, a national monument. Then you’ll walk towards Cerro Concepción along the Gervasoni and Atkinson promenades, with views over the port.\n\nFrom Valparaíso, you’ll continue to Viña del Mar, known as the Garden City. You’ll see the Flower Clock, Reñaca Beach, the waterfront and the Fonck Museum.\n\nYou’ll return to Santiago after the excursion. There’s a stop for lunch, which is at your own expense.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-work-e805e5042bc7",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      }
    },
